{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Publish offline-rhel8 from node1 over HTTP on TCP 8080 with zsh, its dependency closure, repository metadata, and the public signing key.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repository contains 161 RPMs downloaded as zsh's resolved dependency closure. Metadata and the public key exist, Apache is active and listening on 8080, and node2 received HTTP 200 responses for the metadata, detached signature, and key.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4491c899323745ad","cmd-59a44c29d81b4f7c","cmd-aa4f79207bcf4caf","cmd-35dd61031a4441d5"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Sign the repository metadata and RPM packages.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All 161 RPMs passed signature checks after importing the offline key, zsh shows that key's valid signature, and repomd.xml has a valid detached signature.","evidence_ids":["cmd-46883f8889cc4a0c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Enforce repository-metadata and RPM signature verification on node2 using the published key.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 validated and imported the published key, has gpgcheck=1 and repo_gpgcheck=1, and successfully rebuilt its cache and performed package transactions with those settings active.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2cd58cb217314f0e","cmd-8cfc0ea9eea3446d","cmd-411767b015354807","cmd-e73f5b769d37475a"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Give offline-rhel8 priority 10 and all other enabled repositories priority 90 or otherwise lower preference.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The enabled offline repository reports priority 10, while the two other enabled repositories both report priority 90.","evidence_ids":["cmd-411767b015354807","cmd-e77c532563fa405f"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Install zsh on the RHEL 8.8 node2 client from offline-rhel8.","status":"satisfied","summary":"DNF installed zsh 5.5.1-10.el8 from offline-rhel8, and the final audit confirmed the package, signature, executable version, intact files, and HTTP repository location.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e73f5b769d37475a","cmd-e77c532563fa405f"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep zsh reinstallable while every repository other than offline-rhel8 is disabled.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An actual reinstall with all repositories disabled except offline-rhel8 downloaded, verified, and successfully reinstalled zsh.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a0d60b44fc464b26"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Both nodes remained free of failed services and passed package-manager consistency checks. The only notable hygiene issue is an executor-added wildcard Apache listener on TCP 80 in addition to the required 8080 listener; firewall reachability of port 80 was not captured.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence, including client-side HTTP access, valid signatures, enforced verification settings, correct priorities, installation from the offline repository, and a successful isolated reinstall. Operational hygiene is strong aside from Apache's unnecessary additional port-80 listener.","limitations":["No negative tamper test was captured to demonstrate rejection of invalid metadata or RPM signatures; enforcement is supported by the active configuration and successful verified transactions.","No service restart or reboot persistence test was captured, although Apache was directly observed active and enabled."]}
